      "id": "60337445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The General Education Basic Skills and American Institution requirements should be completed prior to taking courses in the major. Major Preparation - Students must meet one of the following criteria: For students for whom English is not the native language, one year of college level English study may fulfill this requirement. One year of college level language other than student’s native language. Demonstrated equivalent competence. One year of college level American Sign Language. Electives in the Major: Elective courses (up to 3 units) from other departments such as World Languages and Literatures, English, Communication Studies, Computer Science, Psychology, Philosophy, Anthropology, and Communicative Disorders can also be taken with prior advisor approval. Any course used to satisfy a major or minor requirement – including support courses, preparation courses, and prerequisites – must be taken for a letter grade (not Credit/No Credit).",
      "contentHtml": "<p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The General Education Basic Skills and American Institution requirements should be completed prior to taking courses in the major. </span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Major Preparation</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> - Students must meet one of the following criteria:</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For students for whom English is not the native language, one year of college level English study may fulfill this requirement.</span></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">One year of college level language other than student’s native language.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Demonstrated equivalent competence.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">One year of college level American Sign Language.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Electives in the Major:</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Elective courses (up to 3 units) from other departments such as World Languages and Literatures, English, Communication Studies, Computer Science, Psychology, Philosophy, Anthropology, and Communicative Disorders can also be taken with prior advisor approval.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Any course used to satisfy a major or minor requirement – including support courses, preparation courses, and prerequisites – must be taken for a letter grade (not Credit/No Credit).</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">﻿</strong></p>"
